<h1>Michilla &quot;Kyla&quot; Blaise</h1>
<p>Chicago Board of Education, District 5b, on the Chicago ballot November 3, 2026. Incumbent. Endorsed by the Chicago Teachers Union.</p>
<p><a href="https://www.blaiseforschoolboard.com/" rel="nofollow noopener">Campaign site (blaiseforschoolboard.com)</a></p>
<h2>Running on</h2>
<p>Blaise says she is running to ensure a quality and enriching education for all students, drawing on her experience navigating CPS as the mother of two CPS students. She emphasizes equity and access, community representation over big-money interests in the first fully elected board, and data-driven approaches to budgets and policy, citing her recent public policy graduate studies.</p>
<h2>Background</h2>
<p>Blaise is a political consultant who founded Blaise and Associates and serves as chief of staff to Cook County Commissioner Frank Aguilar; she began her career on the staff of 46th Ward Alderman Helen Shiller. She was appointed to the board&#39;s District 5b seat in the fall of 2024 after the previous board resigned.</p>
